Subject: The runtime counts changes of its register property cache entries

What this does
  - `JSRuntime.aot_pic_epoch` is incremented whenever a register property cache entry
    (`JSRegPIC`) changes, and the layout export names its offset.

Why we need it
  A compiled function validated every cache cell it speculates on at each call (a load and a compare
  per site: 8-14% of the instructions of a call-heavy kernel). It now remembers the epoch and the
  cache table at which its cells last passed, and skips the validation while both are unchanged.

Why the epoch is sound (every writer of a cell's shape, kind, slot offset, holder shape)
  The fields of a `JSRegPIC` entry and of the holder arrays beside it are written in exactly these
  places, and each one now bumps the epoch:
    - `regvm_pic_entry_reset`: clears the entry and drops the references to its shapes. Every other
      release of a cached shape (a refill, the miss limit, `js_free_regvm_pic` at teardown and when the
      bytecode is freed, which calls it for every entry) goes through it.
    - `regvm_pic_install`: stores a new shape/kind/slot and takes the references (it calls the reset
      first, and bumps again after the fields are set).
    - the two way swaps in `regvm_get_field_ic_x` and `regvm_get_field_ic`, which exchange the primary
      entry and a way (shape, kind, slot and holder together) with no reset.
    - `regvm_global_site_fill` (a global read site's entry) and the generation flush of the global
      cells (`js_gv_site_flush`'s caller), which rewrite `slot_off` of entries of that kind.
  The table itself is allocated once, zeroed (`regvm_pic_ensure`), so a function that validated while
  the table did not exist sees a different table pointer afterwards; the compiled function keys its
  cache on the table pointer as well. A shape that is freed and reallocated at the same address
  cannot pass a stale validation: the entry holds a counted reference to its shape, so the shape is
  freed only when the entry is reset, which bumps the epoch. The only other field written is `misses`
  (an add-transition entry's watchpoint snapshot), which no validation reads.
  A prototype's own shape can change without any entry changing, so a prototype read still tests its
  holder's shape on every call.

